      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Eye and face tracking is increasingly common, and it takes up a lot of avatar parameter space. Plus, now that there is a (rather hacky and incomplete) implementation for VRC+ subscribers, I feel like they'd be a little more incentivized to improve eye and face tracking.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-07-29T01:51:48.879Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "While VRChat technically supports eye and face tracking via OSC, it's not an effective solution. As it stands, the mod for it allowed for much smoother tracking on both the user and other clients. OSC as I understand it has considerable delay on actually tracking your expressions on displaying them on an avatar. With EAC in place, that mod no longer works ofc. I hope that the dev team can implement face tracking natively after the first round of features being added.",
